' Archived PlantUML source retained after the Mermaid diagram in
' docs/LINKO_USE-CASE.md became canonical. This copy reflects the RBAC behavior
' at archival time but is no longer the maintained source of truth.

@startuml
left to right direction

actor "Buyer" as Buyer
actor "Wholesaler" as Wholesaler
actor "Courier" as Courier
actor "Logistics Coordinator" as Coordinator
actor "Administrator" as Admin

rectangle "LINKO Courier & Parcel Tracking System" {
  usecase "Register Parcel" as UC1
  usecase "Calculate Shipping Fee" as UC2
  usecase "Process Payment" as UC3
  usecase "Track Own Parcel (via Order)" as UC4
  usecase "Update Parcel Status" as UC6
  usecase "Assign Courier to Branch" as UC7
  usecase "Manage Service Tiers" as UC8
  usecase "Manage Branches" as UC9
  usecase "Manage Couriers" as UC10
  usecase "Generate Tracking Number" as UC11
  usecase "Record Tracking Log" as UC12
  usecase "View Parcel Details" as UC13
  usecase "Cancel Parcel" as UC14
  usecase "Manage Users" as UC15
  usecase "Manage Businesses" as UC16
}

Buyer -- UC4

Wholesaler -- UC1
Wholesaler -- UC13

Courier -- UC6
Courier -- UC13

Coordinator -- UC1
Coordinator -- UC6
Coordinator -- UC7
Coordinator -- UC9
Coordinator -- UC10
Coordinator -- UC13
Coordinator -- UC14

Admin -- UC1
Admin -- UC6
Admin -- UC7
Admin -- UC8
Admin -- UC9
Admin -- UC10
Admin -- UC13
Admin -- UC14
Admin -- UC15
Admin -- UC16

UC1 ..> UC11 : <<include>>
UC1 ..> UC2 : <<include>>
UC1 ..> UC3 : <<include>>
UC1 ..> UC12 : <<include>>
UC6 ..> UC12 : <<include>>
UC14 ..> UC12 : <<include>>

note right of UC1
  POST /api/parcels permits wholesalers, logistics coordinators,
  and platform administrators. A wholesaler is limited to its
  active sender business; coordinators/admins may book on behalf
  of a sender. Order-backed registration occurs when a wholesaler,
  or a platform-admin override, PATCHes /api/orders/:id/status
  with status "shipped".
end note

note right of UC8
  Edit existing tiers only. No Add/Delete.
end note

note right of UC4
  Read-only, scoped to the buyer's own orders
  (GET /api/parcels/:id buyer scope, API_CONTRACTS section 3.6a).
  No parcel list, no cross-order access.
end note

note right of UC10
  POST /api/admin/users with kind=courier creates the login and
  linked couriers row. Coordinators edit, assign, and deactivate
  existing couriers but do not create courier accounts.
end note

@enduml
